where \({\rm cot}^{2}\)\(\lambda\) is the positive root of the equation \(x^{2}\!-\![{\rm cot}^{2}\ \varphi\!+\!m\ \sinh^{3}\!\psi\ {\rm csc}^{2}\varphi\!-\!m_{1}]x\!-\!m_{1}\ \cot^{4}\!\varphi\!=\!0\) and \(m\ {\tan}^{2}\,\mu\!=\!{\tan}^{2}\varphi\ {\cot}^{2}\!\lambda\!-\!1\).

**17.4.12**: \[E(\varphi\!+\!i\!\psi\!\setminus\!\alpha)\!=\!E(\lambda\!\setminus\!\alpha)\!-\!iE(\mu\!\setminus\!\theta\!\!\circ\!\!-\!\alpha)\] \[+iF(\mu\!\setminus\!\beta\!\circ\!\!-\!\alpha)\!+\!\frac{b_{1}\!+\!ib_{2}}{b_{3}}\]

where \(b_{1}\!=\!{\sin}^{2}\,\alpha\,\sin\,\lambda\,\cos\,\lambda\,\sin^{2}\,\mu(1\!-\!{\sin}^{2}\,\alpha\,\sin^{2}\,\lambda)^{1}\) \(b_{2}\!=\!(1\!-\!{\sin}^{2}\,\alpha\,\sin^{2}\,\lambda)(1\!-\!{\cos}^{2}\, \alpha\,\sin^{2}\,\mu)^{1}\,\sin\,\mu\,\cos\,\mu\) \(b_{3}\!=\!\cos^{2}\,\mu\!+\!{\sin}^{2}\,\alpha\,\sin^{2}\,\lambda\,\sin^{2}\,\mu\) Amplitude Near to \(\pi/2\) (see also 17.5) If \(\cos\,\alpha\,\tan\,\varphi\,\tan\,\psi\!=\!1\)

**17.4.13**: \(F(\varphi\!\setminus\!\alpha)\!+\!F(\psi\!\setminus\!\alpha)\!=\!F(\pi\!/2 \!\setminus\!\alpha)\!=\!K\)

